id:                     E502
trigger_tool:           runtime|test|ld
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        Error loading shared library /[^:]+: Permission denied|\(needed by |do_dlsym failed: Symbol not found.*so=/data/service/hnp
severity:               3
category:               platform, limitation, ohos, musl, security
match_keywords:         dlopen, Permission denied, LD_PRELOAD, needed by, NEEDED, ctypes, CI worker, HNP python, .codesign, binary-sign-tool, release signature, task-private copy
title:                  OHOS CI workers refuse dlopen and LD_PRELOAD of every user-directory shared object regardless of ELF signature while exec-time NEEDED loading still works
root_cause:              The worker loader policy applies to any shared object mapped after process start (dlopen, LD_PRELOAD) for files under user storage directories and rejects it with Permission denied whether the ELF carries a fresh build-time self-signature or the release signature downloaded from the artifact registry. The same freshly self-signed libraries load fine as DT_NEEDED of a process at exec time (verified: the isl C tests passed against the build-time-signed libgmp.so.10 copy resolved from LD_LIBRARY_PATH in build #33895). The interactive device environment is more permissive, so a local dlopen success does not transfer to workers and signature work alone cannot unblock the worker dlopen path.
affected_scope:         Every upstream test that dlopen()s or LD_PRELOADs user-built shared libraries (ctypes/python bindings, plugin hosts, FFI suites) executed on CI workers.
verification_cmd:       Probe each candidate .so in its own ctypes.CDLL process and print one short line per verdict (file tail plus OSError message tail): self-signed private copy, release-signed published file, dlopen target; on a worker all three show Permission denied while binaries whose NEEDED chain includes the same freshly self-signed files execute normally.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           probe-then-route-to-exec-time
rec_description:        Echo one structured short line per load attempt (never head-slice a multi-line traceback buffer) to localize which file and reason the loader reported, then route the required library into the process through the accepted exec-time path; for python ctypes tests use the embedded launcher pattern of E2167.
rec_command:            keep per-file probes line-structured and short (status, errno, last chars of the OSError message, one line per attempt); reference implementation _OHOS_DLOPEN_PROBE_SRC in archives/b/barvinok/0.41.9/conanfile.py
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      escalate-platform-boundary
fallback_description:   When no accepted load path can host the test, report the boundary with the per-file probe matrix, worker ids and build numbers (R41/R43 evidence style) instead of skipping, stubbing or unconditional-pass shims.
fallback_command:       collect the E135PROBE-style short lines from the CI console output and attach them to the PR comment or issue body
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       probe_output\[:[0-9]+\]|\[:[0-9]+\].*(stdout|stderr|traceback)
forbid_1_reason:        Head-slicing a multi-line diagnostic buffer drops the loader reason that rides at the end of the OSError line; thirteen CI rounds lost their forensics to the recipe's own [:400] cap (build #33806) before the probes were restructured.
forbid_1_consequence:   Repeated expensive CI rounds without ever learning which file or reason the loader reported.
forbid_2_pattern:       llvm-objcopy.*\.conan2|binary-sign-tool.*\.conan2
forbid_2_reason:        Conan cache package files are shared immutable inputs; stripping or rewriting .codesign there silently corrupts a release-signed binary and mimics an imaginary platform policy (a diagnostic objcopy aimed at the cache made libgmp.so.10.5.0 unloadable for hours and produced a false "signature expiry" conclusion).
forbid_2_consequence:   Cache-wide corruption misattributed to the platform; recover only via conan remove <pkg> -c and conan download <pkg> -r=<remote>.
forbid_3_pattern:       (skip|XFAIL|xfail).*dlopen|stub.*LoadLibrary
forbid_3_reason:        Skipping or stubbing the dlopen-based upstream test contradicts the path-A full-upstream-test requirement and hides the platform boundary instead of documenting it.
forbid_3_consequence:   Unverifiable test counts and a false-green archive that review and CI audits will reject.
principles:             
doc_file:               doc/E2166.md
similar_to: E135, E077
last_updated:           2026-08-28
source_event:           barvinok 0.41.9 OHOS CI builds #33869 (three-way probe matrix), #33895 (LD_PRELOAD ignored while exec-time OK), #33918 and #33932 on PR #6848
authors: Awstme <awstme@qq.com>
source_pr: !6848
